   "finding": "On 80 m terrain our long-term sunlight matches NASA within about +-8 points with no systematic sign (Connecting ridge 66.7 vs 58.9, Peak near Shackleton 64.5 vs 60.7, Nobile rim 1 64.0 vs 62.2, Leibnitz beta 57.0 vs 64.7, Shoemaker 50.2 vs 50.3). On 5 m terrain at 0.5 m height our values are systematically lower: small-scale relief blocks the grazing Sun. This is a resolution effect, consistent with Barker et al. (2021), not an engine error. Our product uses 5 m terrain and the real hardware height, so it is conservative compared with 60 m maps.",
